arguments.answer:
Proposed fix for the global buffer overflow when decoding FC opcode:
Root cause: the FC path in GetOpInfo (in /src/wasm3/source/m3_compile.h) reads the extended opcode index (opcode & 0xFF) but does not bounds-check against the c_operationsFC array length, allowing reads beyond the end of c_operationsFC when an out-of-range index is encountered.
Minimal fix: guard the FC branch by validating the index against c_operationsFC_count and returning NULL if out of range, otherwise return the proper c_operationsFC entry.
Patch (exact change to /src/wasm3/source/m3_compile.h):

case 0xFC:
  {
    unsigned idx = opcode & 0xFF;
    if (idx >= c_operationsFC_count) return NULL;
    return & c_operationsFC [idx];
  }

Notes:
- c_operationsFC_count is already declared extern in the header (extern const unsigned c_operationsFC_count;).
- This is a minimal, local change and preserves existing behaviour for valid FC opcodes while preventing OOB reads for invalid opcodes.
- After applying the patch, re-run the build and tests (secb repro) to confirm sanitizer no longer triggers for the described case.
